{"results":[{"url":"https://campaignzero.org/research/federal-govt-data-undercounts-police-killings-by-55/","final_url":"https://campaignzero.org/research/federal-govt-data-undercounts-police-killings-by-55/","title":"Fed Gov’t Data Undercounts Police Killings by 55%","description":"Using MPV and other crowd-sourced data, the study found…","language":"en","text":"# /Research\n\nShare\n\nUsing MPV and other crowd-sourced data, the study found:\n\n> “From 1980 to 2018, the NVSS did not report 17,100 deaths (95% UI 16,600–17,600) out of 30,800 deaths (30,300–31,300) that we estimated, accounting for 55.5% (54.8–56.2) of all police violence deaths from 1980 to 2018.”\n\nFind more in: Scholarship\n\nAdditional tags:\n\n# Up Next\n\nView All Research\n\n* 10/01/2021\n\n  Systemic Racism in Police Killings\n* 08/31/2021\n\n  Does Protest Against Police Violence Matter?","author":"Abdul Nasser Rad","published_date":"2021-10-02","latency_ms":174.11670000001322,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}